    "s2": {"x": 3290, "y": 20800, "w": 420, "fill": "blue", "size": "m", "text": "Phone boards\n\nEach phone board imports its desktop template, so the two never drift apart: edit the 1440px board and the 390px one follows.\n\nBelow 1024px the header swaps its navigation for the overlay menu; below 832px every split stacks to one column; cards go one-up below 576px.\n\nBlock chips are off by default here; turn them on with the Show blocks tweak."},
    "s1": {"x": 4560, "y": 0, "w": 420, "fill": "blue", "size": "m", "text": "How to read these boards\n\nEach board is one block-theme template at 1440px, built from the real design-system CSS.\n\nBlue chips name the pattern and blocks that build each section: core/* are WordPress core blocks, ot/* are the theme's custom blocks.\n\nThe header and footer boards are the two template parts; every page imports them.\n\nTurn the chips off with the Show blocks tweak on any board."}
